      "type": "spotlight",
      "item": "tribalpower:iron_grit",
      "text": [
        "Grit is crushed metal waiting for the fire. Shattering raw metal gives **two grit** for each piece, and each grit smelts into an ingot, so every ore gives you twice the metal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Metals",
      "text": [
        "Put a raw metal item, or a silk-touched metal ore, into Echo Shatter: **4 seconds** at **20 Pulse a second** before pack settings, for two grit.",
        "Smelt the grit into an ingot in a furnace, a blast furnace or the Ember Kiln.",
        "Iron, gold and copper have grit of their own. Modded metals ride one **Mineral Grit** item that names its own material, and they light up with no datapack. Netherite is never crushed; it has to be earned in the Nether."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "title": "Gems and minerals",
      "text": [
        "Silk-touched gem ore shatters straight into the gem, at **twice** the ore's own drop:",
        "- Coal, diamond, emerald and quartz give **two**.",
        "- Redstone and lapis give **eight**.",
        "- Modded gems give two.",
        "The gem itself is never an input."
      ]
    },
